{
  "info": {
    "name": "Supabase Auth (GoTrue) Mock API v1",
    "description": "Test collection for the mock Supabase Auth service. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8113. In docker-compose, the service is reachable at http://supabase-auth-api:8113. This is the GoTrue half of the same self-hosted project supabase-api serves, so the anon key (eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.anon.orbit-labs-selfhost) and the service key (eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.service_role.orbit-labs-selfhost) are identical there and the user ids match public.profiles. Seeded sessions carry fixed access tokens so requests can quote a bearer literally: amelia.ortega (aal1, verified TOTP factor), jonas.pereira (aal1, unverified factor) and sync-bot. Seed passwords are listed in settings.json under seed_credentials. Requests labelled '(N expected)' assert an error path.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8113"
    }
  ],
